# D-TASK-SLICE1=A: a cancel or a passed deadline reaches a task busy in a
# recursion that never loops or waits, at the check each call of a function
# that can call itself starts with. A race returns its winner although the
# loser only recurses, a cancelled burner unwinds through its deferred close,
# and a burner that recurses through a function value stops at its
# `task.timeout` with the deadline failure. Without those checks the race
# and the joins never return and the run steps time out.
# Hand-derived expectations, not worker-run.
fixture: a_cancel_or_deadline_stops_a_busy_recursion_at_its_next_call_on_every_tier.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
env: JETPACK_ROOT={work}/jetpack
step: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "7\nclose the burner's marker\nthe burner: cancelled\nthe timed burner: deadline\n"
step: jet run -O1 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "7\nclose the burner's marker\nthe burner: cancelled\nthe timed burner: deadline\n"
step: jet run -O2 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "7\nclose the burner's marker\nthe burner: cancelled\nthe timed burner: deadline\n"
step: jet build -O2 main.jet
exit: 0
step aot: built
exit: 0
stdout: = "7\nclose the burner's marker\nthe burner: cancelled\nthe timed burner: deadline\n"
